r15-fixtures-judge run 4 (2026-10-07, exit 0), kept as -run4 with its script and the pairs it judged (r15-edits/tgc-1-run4.pairs),
on the adopted candidate. Writing the matrix showed that a code-span reading that honoured an escaped backtick as an opener,
or ended a span at a closer of another length, would lose real members, so two member rows were added in both passes
(an escaped backtick before a code span holding a bracket; a code span holding a backtick and a bracket), each checked to
seal on CUR, be refused on D and be lost by exactly its own mutant; the judge of record follows.
